      "entries": [
        "Usilket makes two Strikes with their fist or with a monk weapon. If both hit the same creature, combine their damage for the purpose of resistances and weaknesses."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Force Bolt",
      "category": "passive",
      "placement": "bot",
      "activity": null,
      "traits": [
        "arcane",
        "evocation",
        "force"
      ],
      "entries": [
        "Usilket fires two magic missiles per action spent, dealing 1d4+1 force damage each. They can't spend more actions on this ability than they have free hands. If they use a hand that has Absorbed Force, that hand hurls three missiles instead of two, expending the held energy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Meditative Therapy",
      "category": "passive",
      "placement": "bot",
      "activity": null,
      "traits": [
        "healing",
        "necromancy"
      ],
      "entries": [
        "One of Usilket's most unusual abilities is a technique they learned during a long visit to Jalmeray. Usilket enters a trancelike state for 10 minutes, during which they can attempt to remove a disease or one of the following conditions: clumsy, drained, enfeebled, or stupefied. To remove the disease or condition, Usilket must counteract the disease or condition with a Medicine check. Usilket can attempt to counteract a disease or condition present in another creature, as long as that creature remains adjacent to the witchwyrd during the entire meditation."
      ],
      "frequency": {
        "number": 1,
        "unit": "day",
        "text": null
      }
    },
